# The morning the patio was picked up on the rover.
#
# Twenty-five shots on a 1.5 m by 1.25 m grid, which is a dense survey of a patio
# by any measure and is the density the gate is decided at. Every one of them
# falls on the plane z = 100 + 0.0125y — the ground drops one in eighty away from
# the house wall along y = 6 — so a level read off the derived surface anywhere
# inside them has an arithmetic answer a test can state rather than a number
# somebody copied out of a run.
#
# Nothing here is noisy on purpose. What this file is for is the *budget* of an
# answer, not the residual of one: every shot states the precision the instrument
# reported for it, and what a whole afternoon on one base station is worth is
# stated on the derivation, because no line of this format carries it.
#
# id at frame x y z method fix h-precision v-precision antenna session

